# deploy/hosting.env
#
# Public, tracked, non-secret host facts. Every later Track B deploy task
# (plans 01-07 through 01-09) sources this file for the hostname, static IP,
# instance name and SSH details it needs. This file contains NO credential
# material of any kind — a hostname, a public IP, an instance name, a port
# and a filesystem path only. Do not add a key, token, secret or password
# value to this file out of convenience; add it to a real .env instead
# (gitignored, never tracked).
#
# Plain shell-sourceable KEY=value lines. No `export` keyword needed —
# source with `set -a && . ./deploy/hosting.env && set +a` to export
# everything into the current shell.
#
# --- D-14 resolution (2026-08-24) ---
# CONTEXT.md D-14 asked for a subdomain label (e.g. prodfin.vockell.com).
# The developer's decision at the 01-06 checkpoint was NOT a subdomain:
# "this is not critical path -- just put it at vockell.com/finance and not
# worry about devops." The public URL is a PATH mount on the EXISTING
# vockell.com site, not a new subdomain. Consequences:
#   - PRODFIN_HOST below is the existing apex host, vockell.com — not a
#     new label.
#   - PRODFIN_PUBLIC_PATH records the path prefix the app is mounted under.
#   - No new DNS record was created. vockell.com already resolves to
#     PRODFIN_STATIC_IP. There is no propagation clock in this phase.
#   - The reverse-proxy config in plan 01-09 must add a location/path rule
#     (e.g. Apache ProxyPass /finance) inside the EXISTING vockell.com
#     vhost, reusing its existing TLS certificate — NOT a new bncert-tool
#     run for a new subdomain. See deploy/README.md and the 01-06 SUMMARY
#     "Deviations" section for the full downstream-impact note on 01-09.

# The host the app is publicly reachable through. No new subdomain was
# created — this is the existing vockell.com apex.
PRODFIN_HOST=vockell.com

# Path prefix the app is mounted under on PRODFIN_HOST. Read by the
# Apache reverse-proxy config (plan 01-09) and by any smoke-test script
# that needs the full public URL.
PRODFIN_PUBLIC_PATH=/finance

# Convenience: the full public URL a judge visits. Derived from the two
# values above; recorded directly so later plans don't have to string-
# concatenate it themselves.
PRODFIN_PUBLIC_URL=https://vockell.com/finance

# Static IP already bound to the Lightsail instance and already serving
# the vockell.com apex. [VERIFIED live dig, 01-RESEARCH.md SHP-03]
PRODFIN_STATIC_IP=35.165.60.123

# Current Lightsail instance name. Will change after the snapshot-and-
# restore resize in plan 01-07 (see .claude/CLAUDE.md Constraints).
PRODFIN_INSTANCE=vockell_dot_com_LAMP

# AWS CLI profile and region for any Lightsail/EC2-adjacent call.
PRODFIN_AWS_PROFILE=newaccount
PRODFIN_AWS_REGION=us-west-2

# SSH access to the box.
PRODFIN_SSH_USER=bitnami
PRODFIN_SSH_KEY=~/.ssh/LightsailDefaultKey-us-west-2.pem

# Application process facts.
PRODFIN_APP_PORT=8000
PRODFIN_APP_ROOT=/opt/prodfin
PRODFIN_SERVICE=prodfin.service
PRODFIN_SERVICE_USER=prodfin
